  "guide.ch.0.title": "Prologue: A Note from Maru",
  "guide.ch.0.intro": "\"Hi! I'm Maru. I build things: robots, telescopes, and lately a farm computer. If you're curious, let's be friends. I'll send you the plans one piece at a time.\"",
  "guide.ch.1.title": "1. Chips off the Old Bar",
  "guide.ch.1.intro": "\"Everything starts with processors. My little press squeezes a bar and some quartz into a chip overnight. Wire comes next, and after that... well, you'll see.\"",
  "guide.ch.2.title": "2. Your First Farm Computer",
  "guide.ch.2.intro": "\"A Computer Core, a rack of disks, some power and a Terminal. That's a real network! Put one in your house or a shed and never dig through chests again.\"",
  "guide.ch.3.title": "3. Kegs on Autopilot",
  "guide.ch.3.intro": "\"Machines that feed themselves from storage and empty themselves into it. You set the rules; the network does the lifting. No rule, no work. I promise it won't eat your seeds.\"",
  "guide.ch.4.title": "4. The Network Does the Crafting",
  "guide.ch.4.intro": "\"Ask for five Quality Sprinklers and walk away. The network makes the parts, smelts the bars and hands you the finished thing. Honestly, it's my favourite.\"",
  "guide.ch.5.title": "5. Every Building, One Network",
  "guide.ch.5.intro": "\"Each building's computer works on its own. Now let's join them: a Port by each door, cable across the farm, and every Terminal sees everything.\"",
  "guide.ch.6.title": "6. The Whole Farm Hums",
  "guide.ch.6.intro": "\"The last gadgets I've got: a rack that cooks and keeps your shelves stocked overnight, a disk that holds anything, and a link all the way to Ginger Island.\"",

  "guide.q.open.title": "Open the Journal",
  "guide.q.open.text": "You did it! This journal follows you through every gadget in Stardew Energistics. Each chapter is one of Maru's letters; each goal ticks itself off when you've done it, for you alone, so every farmer in co-op keeps their own journal.\n\nHow to open it: hold the Tinkerer's Journal and press the action button (A on a controller), or press F8. Lost it? Craft another from the crafting menu.\n\nFinish every goal in a chapter and Maru mails you a little thank-you.",
  "guide.q.maru.title": "Make a Friend in the Mountains",
  "guide.q.maru.text": "Maru lives at the Carpenter's Shop, north of town, with Robin and Demetrius. Reach 2 hearts with her and she'll mail you the Processor Press blueprints.\n\nTips: she loves Battery Packs, Gold Bars, Iridium Bars, Diamonds, Cauliflower and Strawberries, and likes Copper and Iron Bars. Talk to her every day too. She also works at the clinic some days.\n\nSee your hearts on the Social tab of the game menu.",

  "guide.q.letter1.title": "Read Maru's First Blueprints",
  "guide.q.letter1.text": "When Maru reaches 2 hearts she sends a letter the next morning. Open it in your mailbox to learn the Processor Press and Copper Wire recipes.",
  "guide.q.press.title": "Squeeze the Day",
  "guide.q.press.text": "How to get: craft a Processor Press from the crafting menu.\n\nHow to use: place it like a Furnace, indoors or out. Hold a bar and use it on the Press; it also takes the other parts from your backpack. Processors are ready the next morning (Iridium takes two days). Click the Press to collect.\n\nIf it says it also needs something, check your backpack for the Refined Quartz, Diamond or processor listed.",
  "guide.q.chip.title": "A Chip off the Old Bar",
  "guide.q.chip.text": "Press your first Copper Processor: put a Copper Bar in the Processor Press with a Refined Quartz in your backpack.\n\nRefined Quartz comes from smelting Quartz (or Fire Quartz) in a Furnace. Quartz turns up all over the Mines.",
  "guide.q.wire.title": "Wired for Adventure",
  "guide.q.wire.text": "How to get: craft Copper Wire (10 per craft).\n\nHow to use: hold the wire and click a floor tile to lay one, or hold the button and walk to lay a line. It joins up on its own. Anything with wire on its tile or right beside it is connected: Computer Cores, Terminals, linked chests and machines. So run the wire up to a chest and stop next to it.\n\nWire is walkable and you can put flooring on top. A pickaxe picks bare wire back up, like a path.",
  "guide.q.tenChips.title": "Chip Collector",
  "guide.q.tenChips.text": "Press 10 Copper Processors in all. Once you've done that and reached floor 20 of the Mines, Maru sends the farm computer blueprints.\n\nTip: a row of Processor Presses works overnight while you sleep.",

  "guide.q.letter2.title": "Read the Farm Computer Letter",
  "guide.q.letter2.text": "Maru's second letter teaches the Computer Core, Storage Rack, Power Rack, Coal Generator, Network Terminal, Chest Link, Copper Disk and Network Wrench.",
  "guide.q.core.title": "A Core Memory",
  "guide.q.core.text": "How to get: craft a Computer Core. It needs a Battery Pack (from a Lightning Rod during a storm).\n\nHow to use: place it inside your farmhouse or a shed. It's the brain: every building gets exactly one. Two Cores on the same wire stop that network until you move one.\n\nClick the Core any time to see what its network holds and how much power is left.",
  "guide.q.disk.title": "Disk-overy",
  "guide.q.disk.text": "How to get: craft a Storage Rack and a Copper Disk.\n\nHow to use: place the rack right beside the Core or another rack, or run wire from the Core to it (wire on its tile or right beside it). Racks beside each other share the connection. Hold a disk and click the rack to slide it in; click with empty hands to take the last disk out, with everything still on it. Each rack holds 4 disks.\n\nA Copper Disk holds 20 kinds and 2,000 items. All qualities of an item count as one kind.",
  "guide.q.power.title": "Power Nap",
  "guide.q.power.text": "How to get: craft a Power Rack and bring Battery Packs.\n\nHow to use: place it beside the Core like any rack, then hold a Battery Pack and click the rack. It holds 4. Each Battery Pack gives {{battery}} power.\n\nThe Core uses 2 a day, each rack and Terminal 1, each Link 0.3, so a small network runs about two weeks on one battery. Out of power, storage still opens but machines and crafting pause. Maru writes 3 days before it runs dry.",
  "guide.q.generator.title": "Keep the Home Fires Burning",
  "guide.q.generator.text": "How to get: craft a Coal Generator (it's built around a Furnace).\n\nHow to use: place it next to the wire, hold Coal or Hardwood and click it to load the whole stack. Each Coal gives {{coal}} power and each Hardwood {{hardwood}}. It only burns when the batteries are empty, so it's a handy backup.",
  "guide.q.terminal.title": "Everything in Its Place",
  "guide.q.terminal.text": "How to get: craft a Network Terminal.\n\nHow to use: place the Terminal and run wire from the Core to a tile right beside it. Click it to open the Storage screen: click items in your backpack to store them, click stored items to take a stack (right-click takes one). On a controller, A takes or stores and the triggers scroll.\n\nThe Craft button opens the crafting menu using everything on the network. Goal: store 10 kinds of items.",
  "guide.q.chest.title": "Chest Friends",
  "guide.q.chest.text": "How to get: craft a Chest Link.\n\nHow to use: run wire up to a chest, fridge or Junimo Chest (beside it is enough), hold the Chest Link and click the chest. Its items now show in the Terminal and crafting can use them, while the chest still opens as normal. Handy for things that can't go on a disk.\n\nThe Network Wrench takes a Chest Link back off.",
  "guide.q.wrench.title": "Out of Sight",
  "guide.q.wrench.text": "How to get: craft a Network Wrench.\n\nHow to use: hold it to see Network View, which shows all wire, hidden or not (F6 toggles it too). Tap a wire tile with the tool button to hide or show it; hold the button to do a whole run at once. It also opens Link settings, paints Heavy Cable and removes Links.\n\nGoal: hide a piece of wire.",

  "guide.q.letter3.title": "Read the Automation Letter",
  "guide.q.letter3.text": "Maru's third letter teaches Machine Links, Shipping Links, Heavy Cable and the Iron and Gold Disks. The Gold Processor needs no recipe: the Processor Press already knows it.",
  "guide.q.goldChip.title": "Good as Gold",
  "guide.q.goldChip.text": "Press a Gold Processor: put a Gold Bar in the Processor Press with a Refined Quartz and a Copper Processor in your backpack.",
  "guide.q.machineLink.title": "Kegs on Autopilot",
  "guide.q.machineLink.text": "How to get: craft a Machine Link.\n\nHow to use: run wire up beside a machine, hold the Link and click the machine. One Link runs every identical machine touching it, so a block of 30 Kegs needs just one. It does nothing until you set it up: hold the Network Wrench and click it.\n\nIn the settings, click items in your backpack to add inputs (top = first choice), use - and + to keep some back (right-click for 10), choose where output goes and when it runs. Copy and Paste share settings between Links. Goal: set up a Link on a powered network.",
  "guide.q.shipping.title": "Ship Shape",
  "guide.q.shipping.text": "How to get: craft a Shipping Link.\n\nHow to use: use it on the farm's Shipping Bin with wire right beside it, or on a Mini-Shipping Bin with wire next to it. Set it up with the Network Wrench like a Machine Link: add items and a keep-back amount. Each night it ships everything above that amount, so \"ship Wine above 50\" just happens.",
  "guide.q.cable.title": "The Long Haul",
  "guide.q.cable.text": "How to get: craft Heavy Cable (10 per craft).\n\nHow to use: lay it like Copper Wire; the two join up. It's made for long runs and outdoors. Hold the Network Wrench and right-click a cable to change its colour: there are 20, the same as chests.",
  "guide.q.ironDisk.title": "Iron Will",
  "guide.q.ironDisk.text": "How to get: craft an Iron Disk. Its recipe takes a Copper Disk, and everything stored on that disk comes along.\n\nIron Disks hold 40 kinds and 8,000 items. Take the old disk out of the rack, craft, and put the new one back in.",
  "guide.q.goldDisk.title": "Heart of Gold",
  "guide.q.goldDisk.text": "How to get: craft a Gold Disk from an Iron Disk (contents kept).\n\nGold Disks hold 63 kinds and 32,000 items.",

  "guide.q.letter4.title": "Read the Autocrafting Letter",
  "guide.q.letter4.text": "Maru's fourth letter teaches the Crafting Rack.",
  "guide.q.craftingRack.title": "Rack 'Em Up",
  "guide.q.craftingRack.text": "How to get: craft a Crafting Rack (it takes a Diamond).\n\nHow to use: place it beside the Core like other racks. Each Crafting Rack runs one autocraft job at a time, so more racks run more jobs. Click it to see its jobs. Goal: a powered network with a Crafting Rack.",
  "guide.q.furnace.title": "Smelt the Roses",
  "guide.q.furnace.text": "Put a Machine Link on a Furnace with wire beside it. Autocraft jobs smelt their own bars in linked Furnaces (and Furnaces touching them), even before you set the Link up. Keep Coal and ore in storage.\n\nIf you set the Link up, it'll smelt for you between jobs too.",
  "guide.q.job.title": "Ask and You Shall Receive",
  "guide.q.job.text": "Open a Terminal and press Autocraft. Pick a recipe you know, choose how many, and the screen shows what it uses or what's missing. Press Start.\n\nThe network crafts the parts first (and smelts bars), every 10 minutes of game time, and puts the result in storage. The Jobs list shows progress, and Cancel stops a job.\n\nOnly the host and split-screen players can autocraft for now.",

  "guide.q.letter5.title": "Read the Linked Buildings Letter",
  "guide.q.letter5.text": "Maru's fifth letter teaches the Network Port, Iridium Disk, Wireless Terminal and Power Feed.",
  "guide.q.iridiumChip.title": "Iridium Ingenuity",
  "guide.q.iridiumChip.text": "Press an Iridium Processor: put an Iridium Bar in the Processor Press with a Diamond and a Gold Processor in your backpack. It takes two days.",
  "guide.q.port.title": "Bridge over Troubled Soil",
  "guide.q.port.text": "How to get: craft two Network Ports.\n\nHow to use: outside, place a Port on a tile right beside a building (any side) and run wire to it. Do the same beside the farmhouse. Run Heavy Cable (or wire) across the farm from one Port to the other, and the building joins the farmhouse network: any Terminal sees both buildings' storage.\n\nEach building still needs its own Core and its own power. Outdoor wire runs on the farmhouse's power. Click a Port to check which building it joined.",
  "guide.q.threeBuildings.title": "Neighbourhood Watch",
  "guide.q.threeBuildings.text": "Join two more buildings to the farmhouse with Network Ports, so one Terminal shows items from three buildings. Sheds, barns, coops, the greenhouse: anything with its own Computer Core inside.",
  "guide.q.wireless.title": "Pocket Computer",
  "guide.q.wireless.text": "How to get: craft a Wireless Terminal (it's built from a Network Terminal).\n\nHow to use: hold it and press the action button anywhere. It opens the network of the building you're in, or the farmhouse's anywhere on the farm or in a farm building.",
  "guide.q.feed.title": "Catch the Lightning",
  "guide.q.feed.text": "How to get: craft a Power Feed.\n\nHow to use: run wire up beside a Lightning Rod or Solar Panel, hold the Feed and click it. Battery Packs it makes go straight into a free Power Rack slot. If every slot is full, they wait in the machine.",
  "guide.q.iridiumDisk.title": "Purple Reign",
  "guide.q.iridiumDisk.text": "How to get: craft an Iridium Disk from a Gold Disk (contents kept).\n\nIridium Disks hold 63 kinds and 128,000 items.",

  "guide.q.letter6.title": "Read the Whole Farm Letter",
  "guide.q.letter6.text": "Maru's last letter teaches the Advanced Crafting Rack, Prismatic Disk and Island Uplink.",
  "guide.q.advancedRack.title": "Chef's Kiss",
  "guide.q.advancedRack.text": "How to get: craft an Advanced Crafting Rack from a Crafting Rack and Qi Gems.\n\nHow to use: place it beside the Core. It runs jobs like a Crafting Rack, and also cooks recipes you know, and smelts in linked Furnaces in every linked building.",
  "guide.q.keepStock.title": "Never Run Out",
  "guide.q.keepStock.text": "In the Terminal's Autocraft screen, pick an item, set the amount, and press Keep. Each night the Advanced Crafting Rack checks your stock and starts a job to top it up, if it can make the whole thing. Press Keep again to stop.\n\nTry \"always keep 100 Speed-Gro\" or a stack of Fried Eggs for the mines.",
  "guide.q.prismaticDisk.title": "Every Colour of Storage",
  "guide.q.prismaticDisk.text": "How to get: craft a Prismatic Disk from an Iridium Disk (contents kept).\n\nIt holds any number of kinds and 512,000 items.",
  "guide.q.uplink.title": "Island Time",
  "guide.q.uplink.text": "How to get: craft two Island Uplinks.\n\nHow to use: you can't run wire across the sea, so place one by your wire on the Ginger Island farm and one by your wire on the home farm (or in a linked building). Every network with an Uplink joins the others, so island chests show up in your farmhouse Terminal.",
  "guide.q.finale.title": "The Whole Farm Hums",
  "guide.q.finale.text": "Finish every other goal in the journal. Every building linked, every machine set up, the shelves stocking themselves. Maru would be proud. Actually, she says she is!",

  "mail.guideCh1.title": "Nice chips!",
  "mail.guideCh1.text": "@!^^You've got the hang of the press! Here's some quartz I had lying around the lab. More chips, more fun.^^   -Maru",
  "mail.guideCh2.title": "Your first network",
  "mail.guideCh2.text": "@!^^A real farm computer! Demetrius pretended not to be impressed, but he asked how it works twice. Here are some spare batteries to keep it humming.^^   -Maru",
  "mail.guideCh3.title": "Automation!",
  "mail.guideCh3.text": "@!^^Machines running themselves... I may have watched your Kegs for a whole afternoon. Take these Gold Bars for the next upgrades.^^   -Maru",
  "mail.guideCh4.title": "It crafts!",
  "mail.guideCh4.text": "@!^^Autocrafting works! I knew it would. Mostly. Here's a Diamond for another Crafting Rack.^^   -Maru",
  "mail.guideCh5.title": "One big network",
  "mail.guideCh5.text": "@!^^Every building on one network. Your farm is officially smarter than my lab. These Iridium Bars should help with the last gadgets.^^   -Maru",
  "mail.guideCh6.title": "Thank you",
  "mail.guideCh6.text": "@!^^You finished every gadget in my journal. Every one! Thank you for believing in my crazy ideas. This shard is the prettiest thing I own, and I want you to have it.^^   -Maru",

  "config.wireUnder": "Wire must be under blocks",
  "config.wireUnder.tip": "Off: wire on a block's tile or right beside it connects. On: only wire under the block counts. Applies after reloading the save.",
  "power.notConnected": "Not connected to a Computer Core. A Coal Generator needs wire on or right beside it that runs to the Core; a Power Rack connects the same way, or by touching the Core or another rack."
}
